PhaseShift: re-arm the L2 stream prefetcher on a late merge. Applies after 0001-l2-stream-prefetch.patch.
New knob (environment, read once): PS_PF_REARM = D sectors (0 or unset = OFF: the bank is then cycle-identical to the 0001-only design; the prefetcher itself still needs PS_PF_DEPTH > 0).
When a demand READ joins (detected in MSHR::enqueue, where pf_late is set; it is drained in CacheBank::tick -- the first version hooked the miss path only and never fired, because late joiners enter the MSHR through the admission path) an in-flight prefetch chain whose prefetch has not returned yet (a LATE merge; first joiner of the chain only), queue the sectors that extend the window to P+D,
P = the prefetched sector joined: the last n = max(PS_PF_STEP, D - PS_PF_DEPTH) sectors up to P+D (D <= DEPTH: just P+D; D = 16 with DEPTH = 8: P+9 .. P+16, so the window stays contiguous).
Hardware cost beyond 0001: none in storage (pf bit per MSHR entry exists; the late bit is used as a once-per-chain guard); one root lookup on the MSHR-join path and pushes into the existing candidate queue.
New counters in the PSPF line: rearm (D), rearm_trig, rearm_queued.

